note /community/ page generator, authored in seeded Omega and compiled by the pinned omc of
note om/hive-page (sha256 in om/hive-page/omc.sha256). It emits four static pages, every byte of
note them held in the text literals below:
note fd 1: the /community/ skeleton (three columns, composer, dialogs, bottom tab bar) that
note community.js fills; fd 3: /community/policy/; fd 4: /community/terms/; fd 5: /community/privacy/.
note No input is read. A failed or short write ends the program with status 1, so a closed output
note descriptor can never publish a truncated page (check.sh exercises that refusal).
note Site rules: first person singular copy, no em or en dash, no inline script or handler,
note classes prefixed cm- (the renderer om/community-render owns cm-code, cm-tag and cm-at).
note /community/ skeleton part 0: from div class="cm" id="cm" data-api="/community/api"
text m0 "<div class=\"cm\" id=\"cm\" data-api=\"/community/api\">\n<div class=\"cm-sky\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>\n<nav class=\"cm-left\" aria-label=\"Community\">\n<p class=\"cm-brand\"><a href=\"/community/\">Community</a></p>\n<ul class=\"cm-menu\">\n<li><a href=\"/community/\" data-nav=\"everyone\">Everyone</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/community/?view=following\" data-nav=\"following\">Following</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/community/?q=\" data-nav=\"search\">Search</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/community/?n=1\" data-nav=\"notifications\">Notifications <span class=\"cm-badge\" data-badge hidden>0</span></a></li>\n<li data-signed hidden><a href=\"/community/?u=\" data-nav=\"profile\" data-profile>Profile</a></li>\n<li data-signed hidden><a href=\"/community/?settings=1\" data-nav=\"settings\">Settings</a></li>\n<li data-mod hidden><a href=\"/community/?mod=1\" data-nav=\"mod\">Moderation queue</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/community/?log=1\" data-nav=\"log\">Moderation log</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"cm-left-h\">Topics</p>\n<ul class=\"cm-topics\">\n<li><a href=\"/community/?tag=omega\">#omega</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/community/?tag=cuda\">#cuda</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/community/?tag=gb10\">#gb10</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/community/?tag=vibecoding\">#vibecoding</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/community/?tag=opencompute\">#opencompute</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"cm-docs\"><a href=\"/community/policy/\">Rules</a> <a href=\"/community/terms/\">Terms</a> <a href=\"/community/privacy/\">Privacy</a> <a href=\"/community/feed/all.atom\">Atom feed</a></p>\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"cm-ghost cm-keys-open\" data-keys>Keyboard shortcuts</button>\n</nav>\n<section class=\"cm-center\" aria-labelledby=\"cm-title\">\n<div class=\"cm-top\">\n<h1 id=\"cm-title\">Community</h1>\n<div id=\"cm-account\" class=\"cm-account\"></div>\n</div>\n<form id=\"cm-search\" class=\"cm-search\" role=\"search\" action=\"/community/\" method=\"get\"><label class=\"cm-sr\" for=\"cm-q\">Search posts and people</label><input id=\"cm-q\" name=\"q\" type=\"search\" placeholder=\"Search posts and people\" maxlength=\"200\" autocomplete=\"off\"><button type=\"submit\" class=\"cm-ghost\">Search</button></form>\n<div id=\"cm-tabs\" class=\"cm-tabs\"><a href=\"/community/\" data-tab=\"everyone\">Everyone</a><a href=\"/community/?view=following\" data-tab=\"following\">Following</a></div>\n<div id=\"cm-intro\" class=\"cm-intro\"><p>I built this space for people building with Omega, CUDA++ and open compute. Every account here was vouched for by a person: you join with an invite from a member and sign in with a passkey, no password. The timeline is newest first, with no ranking, no ads and no trackers.</p><div id=\"cm-signin\" class=\"cm-signin-row\"></div></div>\n<form id=\"cm-compose\" class=\"cm-compose\" hidden>\n<p id=\"cm-mode\" class=\"cm-mode\" hidden><span id=\"cm-mode-text\"></span> <button type=\"button\" id=\"cm-mode-cancel\" class=\"cm-ghost\">Cancel</button></p>\n<label class=\"cm-sr\" for=\"cm-text\">Write a post</label>\n<textarea id=\"cm-text\" name=\"text\" rows=\"3\" placeholder=\"What are you building?\" aria-describedby=\"cm-count cm-hint\"></textarea>\n<details id=\"cm-attach\" class=\"cm-attach\"><summary>Attach a project</summary><label for=\"cm-project\">Path in <code>aien-dev/omega-projects</code></label><input id=\"cm-project\" name=\"project\" type=\"text\" maxlength=\"200\" placeholder=\"projects/your-handle/your-project\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\"></details>\n<div class=\"cm-compose-row\"><span id=\"cm-hint\" class=\"cm-hint\">Ctrl or Cmd and Enter posts.</span><span id=\"cm-count\" class=\"cm-count\">0 / 4000</span><button id=\"cm-post\" type=\"submit\" class=\"cm-primary\">Post</button></div>\n</form>\n<p id=\"cm-status\" class=\"cm-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n<button type=\"button\" id=\"cm-fresh\" class=\"cm-fresh\" hidden></button>\n<div id=\"cm-head\" class=\"cm-head\"></div>\n<ol id=\"cm-feed\" class=\"cm-feed\" aria-label=\"Posts\"></ol>\n<noscript><p class=\"cm-note\">The timeline needs JavaScript. The <a href=\"/community/feed/all.atom\">Atom feed</a> works without it.</p></noscript>\n<button type=\"button\" id=\"cm-older\" class=\"cm-older\" hidden>Load older</button>\n"

note /community/ skeleton part 1: from /section
text m1 "</section>\n<aside class=\"cm-right\" aria-label=\"About this space\">\n<section class=\"cm-panel\">\n<h2>Why this exists</h2>\n<p>X is full of bots. I wanted one place where the people building open compute can talk shop and actually find each other.</p>\n<p>Every account here was vouched for by a person. Joining takes an invite from a member, and a member who invites a spammer can lose the right to invite. Real bots are welcome when a person registers them and they carry a label.</p>\n<p>AI-assisted coding is celebrated here, never shamed. Show what you and your agents built.</p>\n<p>The timeline is chronological. No ranking algorithm, no ads, no trackers.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"cm-panel\">\n<h2>Featured tags</h2>\n<ul class=\"cm-featured\">\n<li><a href=\"/community/?tag=omega\">#omega</a> <span data-tag-count=\"omega\"></span></li>\n<li><a href=\"/community/?tag=cuda\">#cuda</a> <span data-tag-count=\"cuda\"></span></li>\n<li><a href=\"/community/?tag=gb10\">#gb10</a> <span data-tag-count=\"gb10\"></span></li>\n<li><a href=\"/community/?tag=vibecoding\">#vibecoding</a> <span data-tag-count=\"vibecoding\"></span></li>\n<li><a href=\"/community/?tag=opencompute\">#opencompute</a> <span data-tag-count=\"opencompute\"></span></li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"cm-panel\">\n<h2>The rules, short</h2>\n<ul class=\"cm-rules\">\n<li>You are 13 or older.</li>\n<li>Nothing illegal, no harassment, no hate.</li>\n<li>No spam. Automation is registered and labelled.</li>\n<li>No doxxing. No impersonation.</li>\n<li>Coding with AI is welcome.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a href=\"/community/policy/\">Read the full policy</a> and the public <a href=\"/community/?log=1\">moderation log</a>.</p>\n</section>\n</aside>\n<nav class=\"cm-tabbar\" aria-label=\"Community sections\">\n<a href=\"/community/\" data-nav=\"everyone\">Home</a>\n<a href=\"/community/?q=\" data-nav=\"search\">Search</a>\n<a href=\"/community/?n=1\" data-nav=\"notifications\">Alerts <span class=\"cm-badge\" data-badge hidden>0</span></a>\n<a href=\"/community/?u=\" data-nav=\"profile\" data-profile>Profile</a>\n<a href=\"/community/?log=1\" data-nav=\"log\">Log</a>\n</nav>\n<dialog id=\"cm-report\" class=\"cm-dialog\" aria-labelledby=\"cm-report-h\">\n<form id=\"cm-report-form\" method=\"dialog\">\n<h2 id=\"cm-report-h\">Report</h2>\n<p id=\"cm-report-what\" class=\"cm-note\"></p>\n<fieldset><legend>What is wrong?</legend>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"reason\" value=\"spam\" required> Spam or undisclosed automation</label>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"reason\" value=\"harassment\"> Harassment or hate</label>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"reason\" value=\"illegal\"> Illegal content</label>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"reason\" value=\"impersonation\"> Impersonation</label>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"reason\" value=\"other\"> Something else</label>\n</fieldset>\n<label for=\"cm-report-note\">Anything a moderator should know (optional)</label>\n<textarea id=\"cm-report-note\" name=\"note\" rows=\"3\" maxlength=\"500\"></textarea>\n<p class=\"cm-note\">A moderator reviews every report. The person you report never sees who sent it.</p>\n<div class=\"cm-dialog-row\"><button type=\"submit\" value=\"cancel\" class=\"cm-ghost\" formnovalidate>Cancel</button><button type=\"submit\" value=\"send\" class=\"cm-primary\">Send report</button></div>\n</form>\n</dialog>\n<dialog id=\"cm-confirm\" class=\"cm-dialog\" aria-labelledby=\"cm-confirm-h\">\n<form id=\"cm-confirm-form\" method=\"dialog\">\n<h2 id=\"cm-confirm-h\">Are you sure?</h2>\n<p id=\"cm-confirm-text\" class=\"cm-note\"></p>\n<div id=\"cm-confirm-reason\" hidden><label for=\"cm-confirm-input\">Public reason, shown in the moderation log</label><input id=\"cm-confirm-input\" type=\"text\" maxlength=\"200\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div>\n<div class=\"cm-dialog-row\"><button type=\"submit\" value=\"cancel\" class=\"cm-ghost\">Cancel</button><button type=\"submit\" value=\"ok\" id=\"cm-confirm-ok\" class=\"cm-danger\">Confirm</button></div>\n</form>\n</dialog>\n<dialog id=\"cm-revoke\" class=\"cm-dialog\" aria-labelledby=\"cm-revoke-h\">\n<form id=\"cm-revoke-form\" method=\"dialog\">\n<h2 id=\"cm-revoke-h\">Revoke a vouch</h2>\n"

note /community/ skeleton part 2: from p id="cm-revoke-text"
text m2 "<p id=\"cm-revoke-text\"></p>\n<label class=\"cm-check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"cm-revoke-cascade\" name=\"cascade\"> Also revoke everyone this account invited, and everyone they invited</label>\n<p id=\"cm-revoke-warn\" class=\"cm-warn\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n<label for=\"cm-revoke-reason\">Public reason, shown in the moderation log</label>\n<input id=\"cm-revoke-reason\" name=\"reason\" type=\"text\" maxlength=\"200\" autocomplete=\"off\" required>\n<div class=\"cm-dialog-row\"><button type=\"submit\" value=\"cancel\" class=\"cm-ghost\" formnovalidate>Cancel</button><button type=\"submit\" value=\"ok\" class=\"cm-danger\">Revoke</button></div>\n</form>\n</dialog>\n<dialog id=\"cm-keys\" class=\"cm-dialog\" aria-labelledby=\"cm-keys-h\">\n<form method=\"dialog\">\n<h2 id=\"cm-keys-h\">Keyboard shortcuts</h2>\n<dl class=\"cm-keylist\">\n<dt><kbd>j</kbd> <kbd>k</kbd></dt><dd>Next or previous post</dd>\n<dt><kbd>r</kbd></dt><dd>Reply to the selected post</dd>\n<dt><kbd>l</kbd></dt><dd>Like the selected post</dd>\n<dt><kbd>Enter</kbd></dt><dd>Open the selected post</dd>\n<dt><kbd>n</kbd></dt><dd>New post</dd>\n<dt><kbd>/</kbd></dt><dd>Search</dd>\n<dt><kbd>?</kbd></dt><dd>This list</dd>\n<dt><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> <kbd>Enter</kbd></dt><dd>Send the post you are writing</dd>\n</dl>\n<div class=\"cm-dialog-row\"><button type=\"submit\" class=\"cm-primary\">Close</button></div>\n</form>\n</dialog>\n</div>\n"

note /community/policy/ part 0: from article class="cm-doc" id="cm-policy"
text p0 "<article class=\"cm-doc\" id=\"cm-policy\">\n<p class=\"cm-doc-kicker\"><a href=\"/community/\">COMMUNITY</a> / RULES</p>\n<h1>Community rules</h1>\n<p class=\"cm-doc-lead\">I built this space for people building with Omega, CUDA++ and open compute. These rules keep it a place where builders talk to builders. They apply to every post, profile, bot and report.</p>\n<nav class=\"cm-doc-nav\" aria-label=\"Community documents\"><a href=\"/community/policy/\" aria-current=\"page\">Rules</a> <a href=\"/community/terms/\">Terms</a> <a href=\"/community/privacy/\">Privacy</a></nav>\n<section>\n<h2>Who can join</h2>\n<p>You must be at least 13 years old, and old enough where you live to agree to these rules on your own. One person, one account.</p>\n<p>Every account here was vouched for by a person. You join with an invite link from a member and sign in with a passkey, which lives on your device and needs no password. Linking a GitHub account is optional and adds a Verified GitHub badge.</p>\n<p>New accounts start on probation for their first 7 days: 8 posts a day, 1 link and 3 mentions per post, no URL shorteners, and no invites. After that an account is a member: 100 posts a day, 4 links and 8 mentions per post.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Invites are a vouch</h2>\n<p>A member can invite people once their account is 7 days old: at most 3 open links and 5 new ones a week. A link works once, for 14 days. Each profile shows who invited it, and the invite tree is public.</p>\n<p>When you invite someone you vouch for them. If two accounts you invited are suspended for spam or abuse within 30 days, your invites pause until a moderator looks. Within 90 days of a join, the person who sent the invite can revoke that vouch, and moderators can revoke any vouch. A revoked account becomes read-only: it can still sign in, export its data and delete itself. Revoking can also cover everyone that account invited, down the tree. Another member can vouch for a revoked account again, which uses one of their invites.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>What is not allowed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Illegal content.</strong> Nothing that is illegal to publish, and nothing that helps someone break the law against another person.</li>\n<li><strong>Harassment and hate.</strong> No threats, no pile-ons, no attacks on people for who they are. Argue about code and ideas as hard as you like; leave the person alone.</li>\n<li><strong>Spam and undisclosed automation.</strong> No repeated promotion, no engagement bait, no posting by a program from a personal account.</li>\n<li><strong>Doxxing.</strong> No home addresses, private phone numbers, private documents or anything else a person has not made public themselves.</li>\n<li><strong>Impersonation.</strong> Do not pretend to be another person, project or company.</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Bots</h2>\n<p>Bots are welcome when a person stands behind them. A bot must be registered by a signed-in human from Settings, at most 2 per person, and it posts only with its own token. Every bot post carries the label <strong>Bot, run by @owner</strong>, and the owner answers for what it posts. Aien, my site assistant, is labelled <strong>Site assistant</strong> and replies when someone mentions it, a few times an hour at most.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Coding with AI is welcome</h2>\n<p>AI-assisted coding is celebrated here, never shamed. Post what you built with your agents, the prompts that worked and the ones that did not. The only thing I ask is honesty: a person posts from a personal account, and automation says that it is automation.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Reports and moderation</h2>\n<p>Every post and every profile has a Report item in its menu. Pick a reason (spam, harassment, illegal content, impersonation or something else) and add a note if it helps. The person you report never learns who reported them.</p>\n"

note /community/policy/ part 1: from p
text p1 "<p>A moderator reads each report and decides. A moderator can hide a post, dismiss a report, change an account's tier, suspend an account, revoke a vouch, restore a branch of the invite tree or lift an invite pause. Hidden posts disappear from timelines and search. A suspended account cannot post. I appoint the moderators, and I review their decisions.</p>\n<p>If you think a decision about you was wrong, write to <a href=\"mailto:drake@aienos.com\">drake@aienos.com</a> and I will look at it myself.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>The public moderation log</h2>\n<p>Every moderator action is listed in the <a href=\"/community/?log=1\">moderation log</a>: what was done, when, by which moderator and the public reason. Account actions say \"an account\" instead of the handle, so the log does not become a list of names. Private notes between moderators stay private.</p>\n</section>\n<p class=\"cm-doc-date\">Last updated 2026-10-27.</p>\n</article>\n"

note /community/terms/ part 0: from article class="cm-doc" id="cm-terms"
text t0 "<article class=\"cm-doc\" id=\"cm-terms\">\n<p class=\"cm-doc-kicker\"><a href=\"/community/\">COMMUNITY</a> / TERMS</p>\n<h1>Terms of use</h1>\n<p class=\"cm-doc-lead\">The plain terms for using the community on aienos.com. By joining or signing in you agree to them and to the <a href=\"/community/policy/\">community rules</a>.</p>\n<nav class=\"cm-doc-nav\" aria-label=\"Community documents\"><a href=\"/community/policy/\">Rules</a> <a href=\"/community/terms/\" aria-current=\"page\">Terms</a> <a href=\"/community/privacy/\">Privacy</a></nav>\n<section>\n<h2>Who runs this</h2>\n<p>The community is run by me, Drake Stapleton, as an individual. You can reach me at <a href=\"mailto:drake@aienos.com\">drake@aienos.com</a>.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Your account</h2>\n<p>You join with an invite from a member and sign in with a passkey kept on your own devices. Your account belongs to you as a person. Keep your devices locked; anyone who can unlock a device holding your passkey can post as you here. Add a second passkey so you can always get back in. If you link GitHub, keep that account secure too. Bots you register are your responsibility, and their tokens are shown to you once.</p>\n<p>An invite you send is your vouch for that person. Pass each link to one person you know; selling, trading or publishing invite links is not allowed.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Your content</h2>\n<p>You keep every right you have in what you post, including code. By posting you give me a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to store, display, copy and distribute your posts on aienos.com and in its Atom feeds, only as far as running the community needs. The license ends for a post when you delete it, except where another person quoted or replied to it before then and the deletion leaves \"deleted\" in its place.</p>\n<p>If you want others to reuse code you post, say which license it carries. Without one, people may read it and run it here, and should ask you before reusing it elsewhere.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Ending an account</h2>\n<p>You can delete your account at any time from Settings, and everything about it is removed. I may hide posts, limit accounts or suspend accounts that break the rules, and I may close the community or change these terms. A change to these terms is dated on this page before it applies.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>No warranty</h2>\n<p>The community is provided as it is, without any warranty. It may be slow, wrong or offline. Code in posts is written by its authors, not checked by me: read it before you run it outside this page. To the extent the law allows, I am not liable for losses that come from using it.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Copyright notices</h2>\n<p>If you believe a post infringes your copyright, send a notice with the post link, the work you own and your contact details. Notices go to <a href=\"mailto:drake@aienos.com\">drake@aienos.com</a>. My registration of a designated agent with the United States Copyright Office is pending; until it is listed, that address is where notices go.</p>\n</section>\n<p class=\"cm-doc-date\">Last updated 2026-10-27.</p>\n</article>\n"

note /community/privacy/ part 0: from article class="cm-doc" id="cm-privacy"
text v0 "<article class=\"cm-doc\" id=\"cm-privacy\">\n<p class=\"cm-doc-kicker\"><a href=\"/community/\">COMMUNITY</a> / PRIVACY</p>\n<h1>What the community keeps</h1>\n<p class=\"cm-doc-lead\">Exactly what I store about you, why, and how to take it with you or delete it.</p>\n<nav class=\"cm-doc-nav\" aria-label=\"Community documents\"><a href=\"/community/policy/\">Rules</a> <a href=\"/community/terms/\">Terms</a> <a href=\"/community/privacy/\" aria-current=\"page\">Privacy</a></nav>\n<section>\n<h2>What I store</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Your handle, display name, profile text, the projects you list, and the bots you register.</li>\n<li>For each passkey: its public key, credential id, signature counter, the transports your device reports, the name you give it and when it was added and last used. The private key never leaves your device.</li>\n<li>A random 16-byte user id that your passkeys carry, and the account that invited you.</li>\n<li>The invites you create: a note only you see, their status, and who used them. Each invite code is kept only as its SHA-256.</li>\n<li>Your posts, and your interactions: likes, reposts, follows, mutes, blocks, reports you send and your notifications.</li>\n<li>Hashed session tokens. Your browser holds the token; I keep only its SHA-256.</li>\n<li>Only if you link GitHub: your GitHub numeric id, your GitHub login and your GitHub avatar URL.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Linking GitHub asks for no permissions beyond your public profile, and the GitHub token is thrown away as soon as that profile has been read. Without GitHub, your profile shows a letter instead of a picture.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>What I do not do</h2>\n<p>Nothing is sold or sent to third parties. There are no trackers, no ads, no analytics and no third-party scripts or fonts on these pages. Avatars of accounts that linked GitHub are images on GitHub's avatar host: your browser fetches them directly from <code>avatars.githubusercontent.com</code>, with no referrer.</p>\n<p>When a post mentions Aien, my site assistant, its text goes to Aien's model, which runs on my own DGX Spark. It is not sent to an outside AI service.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Cookies</h2>\n<p>Four cookies, all first party: <code>cm_s</code> holds your session for up to 30 days, <code>cm_wc</code> lives for 5 minutes while your device makes or uses a passkey, and <code>cm_st</code> and <code>cm_gp</code> live for 10 minutes during a GitHub sign-in or while you pick a handle after it. No other cookie is set.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Server logs and backups</h2>\n<p>Server logs record the time, the path without its query string and the response status. Network addresses are held only in short-lived memory for rate limiting and are never written to the logs. Backups are kept for 14 days and then deleted.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>What is public</h2>\n<p>Posts, profiles, follower counts and like counts are public, and so are the Atom feeds. Anyone can read them without signing in.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Export and delete</h2>\n<p>Settings has a button that downloads everything stored about you as one JSON file. Settings also deletes your account: you type your handle to confirm, and your account, passkeys, posts, likes, reposts, follows, mutes, blocks, notifications, open invites, sessions and bots are removed for good. Replies other people wrote to your posts stay, and show your post as \"deleted\". Accounts you invited stay, with no inviter shown. If the account was suspended, I keep one salted hash of its passkey credential ids, and of the GitHub id if one was linked, so a ban cannot be undone by deleting.</p>\n<p>Questions go to <a href=\"mailto:drake@aienos.com\">drake@aienos.com</a>.</p>\n</section>\n<p class=\"cm-doc-date\">Last updated 2026-10-27.</p>\n</article>\n"

fn main to int
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len m0 bound 65536
n = write 1 m0 pos sub len m0 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len m1 bound 65536
n = write 1 m1 pos sub len m1 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len m2 bound 65536
n = write 1 m2 pos sub len m2 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len p0 bound 65536
n = write 3 p0 pos sub len p0 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len p1 bound 65536
n = write 3 p1 pos sub len p1 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len t0 bound 65536
n = write 4 t0 pos sub len t0 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
pos = ulong 0
while lt pos len v0 bound 65536
n = write 5 v0 pos sub len v0 pos
if le n 0
ret 1
end
pos = add pos ulong n
end
ret 0
end
